1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,420
Ten hard SAT math questions.

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:09,500
All of them original, all of them built
to feel like the tougher questions on

3
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,900
the real test.

4
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,939
If you're taking the SAT on November 7,

5
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:16,650
this is a good check on where you stand.

6
00:00:17,155 --> 00:00:19,295
Here's how this works.

7
00:00:19,315 --> 00:00:21,815
Pause before every
answer, try it yourself,

8
00:00:21,835 --> 00:00:23,015
and keep score.

9
00:00:23,035 --> 00:00:25,055
They get harder as we go.

10
00:00:25,075 --> 00:00:29,245
At the end, I'll show you what to
study based on the ones you missed.

11
00:00:29,674 --> 00:00:30,614
Question one.

12
00:00:30,634 --> 00:00:34,404
The price of a jacket was
increased by twenty-five percent.

13
00:00:34,594 --> 00:00:38,323
Later, the new price was
decreased by twenty percent.

14
00:00:38,434 --> 00:00:42,483
The final price is what
percent of the original price?

15
00:00:42,915 --> 00:00:44,325
Pause and try it.

16
00:00:51,175 --> 00:00:54,275
The trap is to just do
twenty-five minus twenty,

17
00:00:54,295 --> 00:00:56,625
and pick one hundred five percent.

18
00:00:56,815 --> 00:00:58,555
But percent changes multiply.

19
00:00:58,575 --> 00:00:59,705
They don't add.

20
00:01:00,225 --> 00:01:05,245
A twenty-five percent increase means
multiply by one point two five.

21
00:01:05,265 --> 00:01:09,554
A twenty percent decrease means
multiply by zero point eight.

22
00:01:09,784 --> 00:01:13,764
One point two five times zero
point eight is exactly one.

23
00:01:13,784 --> 00:01:16,325
The price ends up right where it started.

24
00:01:16,345 --> 00:01:22,715
The answer is B, one hundred percent.

25
00:01:23,134 --> 00:01:24,384
Question two.

26
00:01:24,494 --> 00:01:28,514
In the x y plane, line L
passes through the point two,

27
00:01:28,534 --> 00:01:34,513
five, and is perpendicular to the
line four x minus six y equals nine.

28
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:38,943
What is the y coordinate of
the y intercept of line L?

29
00:01:39,439 --> 00:01:40,849
Pause and try it.

30
00:01:47,698 --> 00:01:50,909
First, get the slope of the given line.

31
00:01:51,017 --> 00:01:55,599
Solve four x minus six
y equals nine for y,

32
00:01:55,618 --> 00:01:59,998
and you get y equals two
thirds x minus three halves.

33
00:02:00,017 --> 00:02:02,428
So the slope is two thirds.

34
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:06,199
Perpendicular slopes are
negative reciprocals.

35
00:02:06,219 --> 00:02:10,230
Flip it and change the
sign: negative three halves.

36
00:02:10,741 --> 00:02:12,881
Now use the point two, five.

37
00:02:12,901 --> 00:02:18,321
y minus five equals negative
three halves times x minus two.

38
00:02:18,341 --> 00:02:23,880
Distribute, and you get y equals
negative three halves x plus three,

39
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,081
plus five.

40
00:02:25,101 --> 00:02:29,321
So y equals negative
three halves x plus eight.

41
00:02:29,341 --> 00:02:31,151
The answer is eight.

42
00:02:31,586 --> 00:02:34,726
Desmos shortcut: graph the given line,

43
00:02:34,746 --> 00:02:39,366
then graph y equals negative
three halves times x minus two,

44
00:02:39,386 --> 00:02:43,436
plus five, and click where
it crosses the y axis.

45
00:02:43,881 --> 00:02:45,301
Question three.

46
00:02:45,321 --> 00:02:49,091
A data set of nine numbers
has a mean of twelve.

47
00:02:49,121 --> 00:02:54,020
After one number is removed, the remaining
eight numbers have a mean of eleven.

48
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,690
What number was removed?

49
00:02:56,171 --> 00:02:57,581
Pause and try it.

50
00:03:04,431 --> 00:03:08,851
Any time a mean question
adds or removes a value,

51
00:03:08,871 --> 00:03:11,281
switch from means to totals.

52
00:03:11,351 --> 00:03:14,000
Mean times count gives you the total.

53
00:03:14,458 --> 00:03:18,308
Nine numbers with a mean of twelve
add up to one hundred eight.

54
00:03:18,377 --> 00:03:21,748
Eight numbers with a mean of
eleven add up to eighty-eight.

55
00:03:21,898 --> 00:03:24,118
The difference is the
number that was removed:

56
00:03:24,138 --> 00:03:26,628
one hundred eight minus
eighty-eight is twenty.

57
00:03:27,054 --> 00:03:28,034
Quick sense check.

58
00:03:28,054 --> 00:03:30,833
The mean went down after
the number was removed,

59
00:03:30,853 --> 00:03:34,864
so that number had to be bigger
than the old mean of twelve.

60
00:03:34,934 --> 00:03:36,824
Twenty passes the check.

61
00:03:36,894 --> 00:03:40,224
If you got something below
twelve, something went wrong.

62
00:03:40,754 --> 00:03:42,084
Question four.

63
00:03:42,154 --> 00:03:47,574
The graph of y equals two x
squared plus b x plus fourteen,

64
00:03:47,594 --> 00:03:52,174
where b is a constant, has
its vertex at x equals three.

65
00:03:52,194 --> 00:03:54,724
What is the minimum value of y?

66
00:03:55,168 --> 00:03:56,578
Pause and try it.

67
00:04:03,428 --> 00:04:07,878
The x coordinate of the vertex
is negative b over two a.

68
00:04:08,148 --> 00:04:12,928
Here a is two, so negative
b over four equals three.

69
00:04:12,948 --> 00:04:15,718
That makes b equal to negative twelve.

70
00:04:16,208 --> 00:04:19,628
The minimum value is the
y value at the vertex.

71
00:04:19,648 --> 00:04:23,428
Plug in x equals three: two times nine,

72
00:04:23,448 --> 00:04:26,267
minus thirty-six, plus fourteen.

73
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:29,747
That's eighteen minus
thirty-six plus fourteen,

74
00:04:29,767 --> 00:04:31,468
which is negative four.

75
00:04:31,488 --> 00:04:33,218
The answer is A.

76
00:04:33,696 --> 00:04:36,345
Look at how the wrong choices are built.

77
00:04:36,575 --> 00:04:40,026
Three is the x coordinate of the vertex.

78
00:04:40,056 --> 00:04:42,345
Negative twelve is b.

79
00:04:42,496 --> 00:04:44,835
Fourteen is the y intercept.

80
00:04:44,855 --> 00:04:48,315
Every one of them is a number
you'd find along the way.

81
00:04:48,335 --> 00:04:51,466
That's how hard SAT distractors work.

82
00:04:51,947 --> 00:04:53,127
Question five.

83
00:04:53,147 --> 00:04:55,766
What is the solution to the equation,

84
00:04:55,786 --> 00:04:59,247
the square root of the
quantity two x plus seven,

85
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:01,356
equals x plus two?

86
00:05:01,877 --> 00:05:03,287
Pause and try it.

87
00:05:10,137 --> 00:05:11,627
Square both sides.

88
00:05:11,897 --> 00:05:15,917
Two x plus seven equals
x plus two squared,

89
00:05:15,937 --> 00:05:19,317
which is x squared plus four x plus four.

90
00:05:19,337 --> 00:05:25,397
Move everything to one side: x squared
plus two x minus three equals zero.

91
00:05:25,417 --> 00:05:29,877
That factors into x plus
three, times x minus one.

92
00:05:29,897 --> 00:05:33,027
So x is negative three or one.

93
00:05:33,447 --> 00:05:36,387
But squaring both sides
can create fake solutions.

94
00:05:36,407 --> 00:05:39,547
So check each one in
the original equation.

95
00:05:39,567 --> 00:05:42,986
For negative three, the left
side is the square root of one,

96
00:05:43,006 --> 00:05:44,107
which is one.

97
00:05:44,127 --> 00:05:46,307
The right side is negative one.

98
00:05:46,327 --> 00:05:47,787
Those don't match.

99
00:05:47,807 --> 00:05:49,737
Negative three is fake.

100
00:05:50,187 --> 00:05:52,607
For one, the left side is
the square root of nine,

101
00:05:52,627 --> 00:05:55,407
which is three, and the
right side is three.

102
00:05:55,427 --> 00:05:56,367
That works.

103
00:05:56,387 --> 00:05:58,847
The answer is B, just one.

104
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:02,996
If you picked C, you did the
algebra right but skipped the check.

105
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:07,129
Desmos shortcut: graph both sides.

106
00:06:07,319 --> 00:06:10,930
The graphs only cross
once, at x equals one.

107
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:12,640
Question six.

108
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:17,770
In right triangle A B C,
angle C is a right angle,

109
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:21,119
and sine of A equals five thirteenths.

110
00:06:21,350 --> 00:06:24,520
What is the value of tangent of B?

111
00:06:24,997 --> 00:06:26,407
Pause and try it.

112
00:06:33,257 --> 00:06:34,037
Draw it.

113
00:06:34,057 --> 00:06:36,476
Sine is opposite over hypotenuse.

114
00:06:36,496 --> 00:06:42,716
So from angle A, the opposite side is
five and the hypotenuse is thirteen.

115
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:45,997
That's a five, twelve, thirteen triangle,

116
00:06:46,017 --> 00:06:48,427
so the last side is twelve.

117
00:06:48,921 --> 00:06:50,851
Now switch to angle B.

118
00:06:51,081 --> 00:06:53,651
Tangent is opposite over adjacent.

119
00:06:54,281 --> 00:06:59,781
From B, the opposite side is twelve
and the adjacent side is five.

120
00:06:59,801 --> 00:07:03,170
So tangent of B is twelve fifths.

121
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,691
The answer is C.

122
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:07,140
The trap is A, five twelfths.

123
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,729
That's tangent of A.

124
00:07:08,879 --> 00:07:13,290
Always redraw from the angle the
question actually asks about.

125
00:07:13,694 --> 00:07:14,754
Question seven.

126
00:07:14,774 --> 00:07:19,994
The equation x squared plus y squared
minus six x plus ten y equals two

127
00:07:20,014 --> 00:07:22,904
represents a circle in the x y plane.

128
00:07:23,093 --> 00:07:25,904
What is the length of the circle's radius?

129
00:07:26,355 --> 00:07:27,765
Pause and try it.

130
00:07:34,615 --> 00:07:37,595
This equation is hiding
the circle's standard form,

131
00:07:37,615 --> 00:07:39,665
so we complete the square.

132
00:07:39,735 --> 00:07:42,745
Group the x terms and the y terms.

133
00:07:42,934 --> 00:07:46,545
For x squared minus six x, add nine.

134
00:07:46,735 --> 00:07:50,344
For y squared plus ten y, add twenty-five.

135
00:07:50,455 --> 00:07:53,145
Whatever you add to the
left, add to the right.

136
00:07:53,543 --> 00:07:58,963
That gives x minus three,
squared, plus y plus five,

137
00:07:58,983 --> 00:08:00,883
squared, equals thirty-six.

138
00:08:00,903 --> 00:08:05,192
In standard form, the
right side is r squared.

139
00:08:05,383 --> 00:08:09,473
So r squared is thirty-six,
and the radius is six.

140
00:08:09,663 --> 00:08:11,553
The answer is C.

141
00:08:12,004 --> 00:08:15,894
Thirty-six is the trap for anyone
who forgets to take the square root.

142
00:08:16,164 --> 00:08:19,224
And the center, if they ask, is three,

143
00:08:19,244 --> 00:08:20,774
negative five.

144
00:08:21,243 --> 00:08:22,573
Watch the signs.

145
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,330
Question eight.

146
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:29,300
In the system of equations, three
x minus five y equals seven,

147
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:34,490
and a x plus ten y equals
b, a and b are constants.

148
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:38,060
If the system has
infinitely many solutions,

149
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:40,970
what is the value of a plus b?

150
00:08:41,407 --> 00:08:42,817
Pause and try it.

151
00:08:49,667 --> 00:08:53,406
Infinitely many solutions means the
two equations are the same line.

152
00:08:53,426 --> 00:08:55,757
One has to be a multiple of the other.

153
00:08:56,162 --> 00:08:58,332
Look at the y terms.

154
00:08:58,682 --> 00:09:01,822
Negative five y has to
become positive ten y.

155
00:09:01,842 --> 00:09:05,102
That means multiplying by negative two,

156
00:09:05,122 --> 00:09:06,221
not two.

157
00:09:06,241 --> 00:09:09,862
Multiply the whole first
equation by negative two:

158
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:14,772
negative six x plus ten y
equals negative fourteen.

159
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:16,170
Match it up.

160
00:09:16,190 --> 00:09:19,610
a is negative six, and
b is negative fourteen.

161
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:22,650
So a plus b is negative twenty.

162
00:09:22,670 --> 00:09:27,170
If you multiplied by positive two,
you'd get the wrong signs everywhere.

163
00:09:27,190 --> 00:09:29,639
That's exactly what this
question is testing.

164
00:09:30,071 --> 00:09:31,131
Question nine.

165
00:09:31,151 --> 00:09:35,411
The system y equals x squared
minus six x plus eleven,

166
00:09:35,431 --> 00:09:39,690
and y equals two x plus
k, where k is a constant,

167
00:09:39,710 --> 00:09:42,491
has exactly one real solution.

168
00:09:42,511 --> 00:09:44,441
What is the value of k?

169
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,330
Pause and try it.

170
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:59,600
Set the two equations equal: x squared
minus six x plus eleven equals two x plus

171
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,560
k.

172
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:07,239
Move everything to one side: x squared
minus eight x plus eleven minus k equals

173
00:10:07,259 --> 00:10:08,259
zero.

174
00:10:08,491 --> 00:10:11,741
Exactly one solution
means the discriminant,

175
00:10:11,971 --> 00:10:15,351
b squared minus four a c, equals zero.

176
00:10:15,371 --> 00:10:21,790
That's sixty-four minus four
times eleven minus k equals zero.

177
00:10:21,810 --> 00:10:27,661
So sixty-four minus forty-four
plus four k equals zero.

178
00:10:27,731 --> 00:10:32,501
Twenty plus four k equals zero,
and k equals negative five.

179
00:10:33,028 --> 00:10:35,887
Desmos shortcut: type both equations,

180
00:10:35,907 --> 00:10:41,047
add a slider for k, and drag until
the line just touches the parabola.

181
00:10:41,067 --> 00:10:44,087
It happens at k equals negative five,

182
00:10:44,107 --> 00:10:46,558
touching at the point four, three.

183
00:10:46,962 --> 00:10:47,742
Last one.

184
00:10:47,762 --> 00:10:48,822
The hardest.

185
00:10:48,842 --> 00:10:55,251
The function Q of t equals three hundred
times one point two one to the t,

186
00:10:55,281 --> 00:10:59,341
models a quantity t years
after it was first measured.

187
00:10:59,361 --> 00:11:02,982
Which function is equivalent to Q of t,

188
00:11:03,002 --> 00:11:08,172
and shows that the quantity increases
by ten percent every half year?

189
00:11:08,634 --> 00:11:09,654
Pause and try it.

190
00:11:09,674 --> 00:11:11,444
Take a little longer on this one.

191
00:11:20,211 --> 00:11:23,910
A ten percent increase means
multiplying by one point one.

192
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:28,911
And every half year means the
exponent should count half years.

193
00:11:28,931 --> 00:11:31,510
In t years, there are two t half years.

194
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:35,860
So we're looking for one point
one, raised to the two t.

195
00:11:36,350 --> 00:11:37,640
But is it equivalent?

196
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:41,010
One point one squared
is one point two one.

197
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:46,720
So one point one to the two t is the
same as one point two one to the t.

198
00:11:46,749 --> 00:11:47,770
They're equal.

199
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,360
The answer is A.

200
00:11:49,838 --> 00:11:51,168
The trap is B.

201
00:11:51,278 --> 00:11:56,048
It's tempting to think half of twenty-one
percent is ten point five percent.

202
00:11:56,398 --> 00:11:58,538
But growth compounds.

203
00:11:58,558 --> 00:12:02,018
One point one zero five squared
is about one point two two,

204
00:12:02,038 --> 00:12:03,658
not one point two one.

205
00:12:03,678 --> 00:12:05,528
So B isn't equivalent.

206
00:12:05,986 --> 00:12:08,325
C and D aren't equivalent either.

207
00:12:08,345 --> 00:12:14,085
You can confirm in Desmos: type the
original and each choice using x instead of

208
00:12:14,105 --> 00:12:18,166
t, zoom out, since the values
start at three hundred,

209
00:12:18,186 --> 00:12:21,276
and only A lands exactly on top.

210
00:12:21,662 --> 00:12:22,562
That's ten.

211
00:12:22,582 --> 00:12:24,032
Count up your score.

212
00:12:24,381 --> 00:12:28,072
Now, more useful than the
score is which ones you missed.

213
00:12:28,590 --> 00:12:32,759
Questions two and eight are
algebra: lines and systems.

214
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:37,209
Questions four, five, nine,
and ten are advanced math:

215
00:12:37,229 --> 00:12:40,170
quadratics, radicals, and exponentials.

216
00:12:40,190 --> 00:12:45,410
Together, algebra and advanced math make
up about seventy percent of the math

217
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:49,080
section, so misses there
are the first thing to fix.

218
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:53,337
Questions one and three are
problem solving and data analysis:

219
00:12:53,357 --> 00:12:55,408
percents and statistics.

220
00:12:55,518 --> 00:12:59,087
Questions six and seven
are geometry and trig.

221
00:12:59,198 --> 00:13:01,778
If those were your misses,
review percent change,

222
00:13:01,798 --> 00:13:06,088
means, right triangles, and
completing the square for circles.

223
00:13:06,534 --> 00:13:09,384
And notice the pattern across all ten.

224
00:13:09,494 --> 00:13:12,674
The wrong answers were
numbers from the right work:

225
00:13:12,694 --> 00:13:17,194
the vertex instead of the
minimum, r squared instead of r,

226
00:13:17,214 --> 00:13:20,263
the fake solution you forgot to check.

227
00:13:20,853 --> 00:13:26,424
On hard questions, finish by rereading
exactly what the question asks for.

228
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:31,100
Every question in this video
was written for this video,

229
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:33,530
in the style of the real test.

230
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:38,620
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

231
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,610
skill and difficulty.

232
00:13:41,072 --> 00:13:42,692
If you're testing on November 7,

233
00:13:42,712 --> 00:13:43,532
good luck.

234
00:13:43,552 --> 00:13:45,132
If this helped, subscribe.

235
00:13:45,152 --> 00:13:48,562
There's a new set like
this before every SAT date.
